      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "385bd295b744542918a16bb6e1a2637e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"7-engines\">7. Engines</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Say your team's rollup runs in three places. Analysts try it on DuckDB\nin a notebook, the service that serves it runs Polars, and the warehouse\nthat stores the history runs Spark. The proof was made once, on one\nplan. Nobody wants to redo it for each engine, and nobody wants to\nfind out at 3 a.m. which engine reads a plan differently.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We'll prove one query, run it on DuckDB, Polars and Spark, write it as\nSQL for Spark and Snowflake, and then ask an engine for something it\ncan't run. Each refusal names an exit, and we'll follow them.</span>\n<h2 id=\"1-one-query-proved-once\">1. One query, proved once</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We total each customer's order quantities. A sum of integers can\noverflow, so the verdict may come with checks that the run makes on the\ndata, and it says so:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bkHC",
      "code_hash": "a7d3eca2c3f441174d026ec1edcf5802",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<pre class='text-xs'>&lt;Verdict.PROVED_WITH_CHECKS: &#x27;proved_with_checks&#x27;&gt;</pre>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "lEQa",
      "code_hash": "a5d530ea24136403c3b7cd28160a4b4c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"2-run-it-where-your-data-lives\">2. Run it where your data lives</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>report.run(con, engine, route=\"auto\")</code> runs the checked plan on an\nengine. Before it runs, <code>route=\"auto\"</code> asks how the proof reaches that\nengine: the plan's class there is <code>exact</code> (every result the engine can\ngive, the reference allows), <code>observed</code>, <code>shim</code> (the plan is rewritten by\na proved translation first) or <code>refused</code>. We run the rollup on each of\nthe three:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
