          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">DuckDB gives what the reference gives, <code>exact</code>. Polars and Spark need a shim:\nSpark adds integers in a wider decimal and checks the result fits again, and Polars writes the sum of no rows as NULL. Each shim carries its own\nproof or test evidence, and the route says which.</span>\n<h2 id=\"3-the-same-plan-as-sql\">3. The same plan as SQL</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A warehouse runs SQL. <code>report.to_sql(dialect)</code>\nwrites the checked plan for DuckDB, Spark or Snowflake. Spark's version\nkeeps the overflow check of the sum, raising an error where the sum\nleaves 64 bits:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
