      "id": "ROlb",
      "code_hash": "0b1820f19c5c60393befc24956b14afb",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Some refusals name a rewrite as their exit. Spark and Snowflake take\ntheir <code>ln</code> from Java's <code>StrictMath</code> and an undocumented libm, and Lean's\nmodel uses C's. The writer refuses the step and says so:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "qnkX",
      "code_hash": "86290fa4d58c02d5df824ca3fb013602",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": [
        {
          "type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": "snowflake: WriterUnsupported: Snowflake's LN is not documented to be C's libm, which the Lean model uses; rewrite this step\n",
          "mimetype": "text/plain"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "TqIu",
      "code_hash": "fe91a2de0e8b4e310ceaf210e011b928",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">A refusal of an engine or a writer names its exit: run the plan on\nDuckDB, or rewrite the step. The\n<a href=\"https://github.com/AlexanderNenninger/substrait-lean/blob/v0.9.0/docs/stability.md#engines\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">engines page</a>\nsays which engine runs what, and why.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">You can now prove a query once and run it on DuckDB, Polars or Spark,\nhand the same plan to a warehouse as SQL, and read a refusal as\ndirections. The last chapter,\n<a href=\"?file=08_dbt.py\">Your dbt project</a>, proves the tests of a dbt project\nbefore its models run. The\n<a href=\"https://github.com/AlexanderNenninger/substrait-lean/blob/v0.9.0/docs/tasks.md\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">guide</a>\ncovers every feature in more detail.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
